parallel.task:
Explore the '{target.area}' area for this request: {task}

Focus: {target.focus}

Investigate relevant files, entry points, data flow, existing patterns, constraints, and risks. Write your findings to .explore/{target.area}.md in the project (create the directory if needed). Then return a one-paragraph summary including the file path.

chain.task:
Write a decision-complete execution plan for: {task}

Before writing anything, read the write-plan SKILL.md in full and follow its plan output format exactly. Read every file under .explore/ as gathered context; make reasonable assumptions instead of asking questions, and record them under Risks and Assumptions. Derive a slug and write .plan/<slug>/task.md in the required format. Do not write source code.

External research input (may say none needed):
{outputs.externalResearch}

Return the absolute path of task.md and a one-sentence plan summary.

Review this plan for: {task}

Planner handoff:
{outputs.plan}

Read the actual .plan/<slug>/task.md at the path in the handoff. Challenge assumptions, find gaps, risks, missing edge cases, wrong wave sequencing, and sub-tasks without checkable completion criteria. Report concrete problems and the safest next move. Advisory only, do not edit files.

Revise the plan for: {task}

Oracle review:
{outputs.planReview}

Read the current .plan/<slug>/task.md and the write-plan SKILL.md. Fold in the oracle's valid findings, keep the required format, and update .plan/<slug>/task.md in place. Do not write source code.

Return the absolute path of task.md and a one-sentence summary of what changed.

Implement the full approved plan for: {task}

Plan handoff:
{outputs.planFinal}

Read .plan/<slug>/task.md at that path and execute every wave in order, one sub-task at a time. You are the sole writer for the project. Run focused validation after each wave and report changed files, commands run with exit codes, failures, and remaining issues.

Triage these three reviews for: {task}

Correctness review:
{outputs.reviewCorrectness}

Readability review:
{outputs.reviewReadability}

Maintainability review:
{outputs.reviewMaintainability}

Decide which findings are worth fixing now, which to defer, and which to ignore. For each accepted fix give the exact file, the problem, and the smallest safe change. Advisory only; do not modify project/source files.

Apply only the accepted fixes from the oracle triage for: {task}

{outputs.fixes}

You are the sole writer for the project. Do not expand scope beyond the accepted fixes. Run focused validation and report changed files, commands run with exit codes, failures, and remaining issues.
